WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.627
Kirk's fixed point problem.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.658
Rotating a disk moves no two points apart.

3
00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:08.158
Does reflexivity alone guarantee a fixed point?

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.590
A smallest bad set yields a tree whose branch breaks compactness.

5
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.227
Claimed: yes, in every reflexive Banach space.

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.127
Main theorem Lean-checked.
